1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,680
Actually, I can understand.

2
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,680
That kid

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,160
really deserved the championship.

4
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,880
But

5
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,210
what happened next?

6
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,240
Did she ever come back?

7
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,000
No, she didn't.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,760
She texted me saying
she wasn't feeling well

9
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,800
and went home first.

10
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,760
So that means

11
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,280
Shen Xi and Gao Yuhai did see each other,

12
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:31,940
but didn't even say hi.

13
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,040
That's exactly right.

14
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,920
When Li Fang asked me,

15
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,640
he only asked if they had seen each other.

16
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,040
I thought about it later.

17
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,370
They did see each other,

18
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,000
but they didn't speak

19
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,360
or interact.

20
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:45,680
If that's the case,

21
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,040
I'm really sorry.

22
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,200
I held up your work

23
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:49,440
and didn't help much.

24
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,760
Not at all. Not at all.

25
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,120
We really appreciate

26
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,880
your and Mr. Meng's cooperation.

27
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,340
It was still helpful to us.

28
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,280
Well,

29
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,320
I have a question for Ms. Mu.

30
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,240
Is it possible that Shen Xi knew Gao Yuhai

31
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,560
before the competition?

32
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:05,600
Do you know anything

33
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,260
about this?

34
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:07,280
Well,

35
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,840
I'm really sorry,

36
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:09,770
but I don't know.

37
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,400
Because before the competition,

38
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,760
I didn't know Shen Xi or Mr. Gao either.

39
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:14,970
Understood.

40
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,760
Then do you know

41
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:17,840
Mr. Li Fang?

42
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,920
I only met him during the competition too.

43
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,120
I don't know him well.

44
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:22,850
Understood.

45
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:25,720
Any other questions?

46
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,360
No.

47
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,900
Thanks for your time, you two.

48
00:01:29,039 --> 00:01:31,440
We'll contact you
if we need anything else.

49
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,280
Jiang, please see them out.

50
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:32,960
Sure. Okay.

51
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:33,479
Alright.

52
00:01:33,479 --> 00:01:34,740
We'll be leaving then.

53
00:01:34,759 --> 00:01:35,289
Goodbye.

54
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:38,759
Goodbye, Ms. Mu.

55
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:39,420
Okay, okay.

56
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:40,360
Goodbye.

57
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,440
What do you think?

58
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,160
It all sounds fine.

59
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:55,200
Shen Xi didn't place in the competition,

60
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,280
so she left the celebration banquet early.

61
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,460
But there's one thing.

62
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,680
Remember when we first asked Shen Xi

63
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,240
if she knew Gao Yuhai,

64
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,500
she said she had only seen him
in newspapers and magazines?

65
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:10,840
If what Ms. Mu described

66
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,160
is true,

67
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,440
Shen Xi should have
a deep impression of Gao Yuhai

68
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,320
and that incident.

69
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,360
Right.

70
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,520
Why would she lie?

71
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,500
We need to question Shen Xi again.

72
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,700
These cops are here again.

73
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,000
They just won't stop.

74
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,450
If this keeps up,

75
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,810
Shen Xi will break down.

76
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,760
Officers,

77
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,440
you're looking for me again.

78
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,240
Is there any other problem?

79
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,360
Ms. Shen, here's the thing.

80
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,600
Don't call me Ms. Shen.

81
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,800
Just call me Shen Xi.

82
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:52,610
It sounds more natural.

83
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:53,680
Okay, Shen Xi.

84
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,240
Here's the thing.

85
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,000
We mainly want to ask you,

86
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,400
did you see Gao Yuhai

87
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,600
before the accident?

88
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,880
This question...

89
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,200
I think you already asked it

90
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,530
last time you were here.

91
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:06,880
Yes.

92
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,280
But this time,

93
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:10,240
we mainly want to hear your

94
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,300
confirmed answer.

95
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,570
I didn't see him.

96
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,480
Do you know

97
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,280
a Ms. Mu?

98
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,200
Ms. Mu?

99
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,040
I have an impression.

100
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,200
She was the choreographer

101
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,260
for our dance competition that year.

102
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,560
According to Ms. Mu's description,

103
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,960
you saw Gao Yuhai

104
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,520
on the day of the celebration party.

105
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,280
Do you need us to help you recall?

106
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:49,000
I don't think

107
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,660
that counts as seeing him.

108
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,760
I was in a terrible mood

109
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,160
that day.

110
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,120
After Mr. Gao arrived,

111
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,640
I barely looked up.

112
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,800
I don't even remember what he looks like.

113
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,280
Strictly speaking,

114
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,600
I did see him.

115
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,080
But to me,

116
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,280
it doesn't count.

117
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:48,560
Jiang'er.

118
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,560
You're early today.

119
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,360
Captain Li, come here for a second.

120
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,880
I made a major discovery.

121
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:53,960
Look.

122
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:56,560
I repeatedly studied Bai Xiaosi's videos

123
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:57,720
and found that

124
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,080
there is a person in all of them.

125
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,080
Look, right here.

126
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,480
And this one, Captain Li.

127
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:02,960
Look.

128
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,170
Including this one.

129
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,960
This is the video where Bai Xiaosi

130
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,840
first pretended to be a traffic cop

131
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,880
and went viral.

132
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:10,940
Right here.

133
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,680
This SUV is at...

134
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,520
Where's the mysterious man?

135
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,560
Don't rush.

136
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,010
Three, two, one.

137
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,640
Three, two, one.

138
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:21,680
Right here.

139
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,970
Captain Li, isn't this a major discovery?

140
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:29,120
A mysterious man.

141
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,840
A yellow SUV.

142
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:34,340
At least it proves
that Bai Xiaosi's case is not simple.

143
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,960
Did you stay up all night?

144
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,640
Your dark circles are
heavier than a panda's.

145
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,370
It's fine. I'll just take a nap.

146
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,440
So, Captain Li,

147
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,880
what's our next plan?

148
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,560
I'll ask later.

149
00:05:51,159 --> 00:05:51,960
Captain Weng.

150
00:05:52,159 --> 00:05:54,320
How was Bai Xiaosi dealt with?

151
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,600
He was detained

152
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,780
for seven days.

153
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,620
He should be out by now.

154
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,100
Did you find anything?

155
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,400
Call him to the station.

156
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,930
I have something to ask him.

157
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,240
No need.

158
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,080
Find their home address.

159
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:07,940
We'll go there.

160
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,680
It's a good chance to see what this kid's

161
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,210
family background is like.

162
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:11,640
Okay.

163
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,560
Si,

164
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:19,960
Si,

165
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,200
still sleeping?

166
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,020
Bai Xiaosi.

167
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:37,540
Ze, you're messing with me again.

168
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,480
You were only in there for a few days.

169
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,680
Is it really that bad?

170
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,680
Ze, you really don't know.

171
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,040
That place is simply not for humans.

172
00:06:45,159 --> 00:06:47,120
Meals were just steamed buns and cabbage,

173
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,960
not a drop of oil in sight.

174
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,360
Sleeping space was the size of a palm.

175
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,880
I was woken up

176
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:54,810
for duty right after I fell asleep.

177
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,520
Since I got back,

178
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,920
I've been recovering for three days
and I'm still not over it.

179
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:01,080
The police haven't looked for you again,
right?

180
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,080
Are you completely in the clear now?

181
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,640
Nothing from the police.

182
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:08,040
I was locked up for 15 days.

183
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,160
But something big

184
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,160
happened at home.

185
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,520
My grandpa almost beat me to death
with a belt

186
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,850
and scolded me for days.

187
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,320
Tell me if you have any difficulties.

188
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:15,980
Go to sleep.

189
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:27,400
Is this it?

190
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,200
Let's go.

191
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,960
Who is it?

192
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,520
Grandpa, open the door.

193
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:40,640
Someone's here.

194
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,280
Si,

195
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,560
you're awake.

196
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,480
Your grandpa went out to buy medicine.

197
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,140
Pour grandma a glass of water.

198
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,460
Here, Grandma.

199
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:03,200
Who is it this early in the morning?

200
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:07,920
Officers.

201
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,560
I'm... I'm just at home.

202
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,640
I've been behaving...

203
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:12,720
pretty well.

204
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:15,520
Don't be nervous,

205
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:16,200
buddy.

206
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,690
We just want to ask you a few questions.

207
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,060
Are your parents home?

208
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,040
My grandma

209
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,480
is in poor health.

210
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,000
My grandpa went to buy medicine for her.

211
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,000
Come, take a look at this.

212
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:43,960
Bai Xiaosi.

213
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,480
These are the videos of the three times

214
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:48,760
someone impersonated a traffic cop
based on your description.

215
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,020
After our comparison,

216
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,280
the same person appeared
in all three videos.

217
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,760
The one we circled in red.

218
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,280
He's wearing a hat, mask,

219
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,610
and sunglasses.

220
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,500
Tell us who this person is.

221
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,840
I-I don't know him.

222
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,010
I don't know him.

223
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,090
Are you sure you don't know him?

224
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,890
Bai Xiaosi, let me tell you,

225
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:10,410
this person is connected to a murder case.

226
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,560
If you know something and don't report it,

227
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,640
and he really committed a crime,

228
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,760
you'll be charged
with harboring a criminal.

229
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,080
That won't be as simple

230
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:17,880
as a few days in detention.

231
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:19,410
Think it through yourself.

232
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,860
What are you doing?

233
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,400
Standing here

234
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:45,800
right now,

235
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,200
my hands...

236
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,840
even trembling slightly.

237
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,200
In this car accident,

238
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,880
I lost not only

239
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:57,000
a life mentor,

240
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,680
but also a father.

241
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:01,800
When I left

242
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,780
the company this morning,

243
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:07,240
his warmth still lingered
on the mahogany chair

244
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,000
in the chairman's office.

245
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,960
The strategic planning map
at the end of the corridor

246
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,480
is still hanging on the wall.

247
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,320
But

248
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:15,240
the figure who led us

249
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:17,240
to the top of the industry

250
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:21,240
will never open the door
of the conference room again.

251
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,280
He always said that

252
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,040
there is no such word as "surrender"

253
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,500
in Wending's dictionary.

254
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,120
Now,

255
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,880
the baton has been passed to us.

256
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,640
No one

257
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,880
can let the name Gao Yuhai gather dust.

258
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,440
As

259
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,420
the future son-in-law of the Gao family,

260
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:50,000
I know better than anyone here

261
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:52,380
the softness hidden under his iron fist.

262
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,680
There was always a box of throat lozenges

263
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,920
in his office drawer.

264
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:00,320
Because he knew

265
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:03,360
our employees would get sore throats
from working overtime at night.

266
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:05,000
When an employee's child got into college,

267
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,560
he was even happier than the employee.

268
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:18,800
Such a man

269
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,260
shouldn't have left so suddenly.

270
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,800
But everyone,

271
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,400
please believe

272
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,760
that I will carry his instructions

273
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,960
and the backbone of Wending's people

274
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:33,520
to let this giant ship of the group
brave the wind and waves.

275
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,120
Good, good.

276
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,200
Enough.

277
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,160
Feng Shu,

278
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,660
what right do you have
to speak for my father?

279
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,200
Everyone,

280
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,000
I guess you don't know.

281
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:47,200
He and I

282
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,980
have never been together.

283
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:52,360
The one standing here pretending to mourn

284
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,560
is just a villain

285
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:57,160
who has always dreamed of becoming
the Gao family's son-in-law.

286
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,080
Get out of the way.

287
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,600
Didn't you say

288
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:07,080
my father was your life mentor?

289
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,280
Then who

290
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,680
united the shareholders yesterday

291
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,760
to strip me of my power as the heir?

292
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,400
I am Gao Yuhai's only daughter.

293
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,040
My dad holds

294
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,500
more than 60% of the shares
in Wending Group.

295
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,920
I am the rightful heir

296
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,930
to the chairman's seat.

297
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,960
But you haven't worked a single day.

298
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:30,920
Can you do it?

299
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,010
You should leave it to Mr. Feng.

300
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,160
Mr. Feng is young and promising.

301
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,560
He will definitely do better than you.

302
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:36,400
You're just a little girl.

303
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,600
Why are you trying to be brave?

304
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:40,240
Do you think running a business
is like shopping at a mall?

305
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:40,960
Exactly.

306
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,320
I still think Mr. Feng

307
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,600
is the one who can take on
this heavy responsibility.

308
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,160
Yeah, why are you trying to be brave?

309
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:45,960
Exactly.

310
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:47,520
Can a little girl

311
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:49,320
handle it?

312
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:51,160
Mr. Feng is more suitable.

313
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,400
Everyone,

314
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,320
blood is thicker than water.

315
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,680
This is an eternal truth.

316
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,280
Many of you here

317
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:03,530
are Wending veterans
who fought alongside my father

318
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:06,600
and watched me grow up.

319
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:11,000
I know you might have issues with me,

320
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,260
and I know my relationship with my father

321
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,160
was never that good.

322
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,200
But whatever conflicts we had,

323
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:23,690
that's a family matter
between father and daughter.

324
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,840
Now,

325
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,680
he's gone.

326
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:36,440
As his only daughter,

327
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:39,480
I will never let his life's work

328
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,140
fall into the hands of others.

329
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,840
And I will never let

330
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,520
anyone with wild ambitions

331
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,200
encroach on his interests.

332
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,080
Please believe

333
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,800
that I will do my utmost

334
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,960
to work with you all

335
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,890
to make Wending better and better.

336
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,040
Please believe in

337
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,570
a daughter's determination
to protect her family's business.

338
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,000
Please believe in me,

339
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:06,720
okay?

340
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,440
So,

341
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:11,040
that person approached you

342
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,560
and asked you
to impersonate a traffic cop?

343
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,840
Exactly.

344
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,200
What was the purpose?

345
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,840
I don't know about that.

346
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:19,800
He gave me money

347
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,240
and a motorcycle.

348
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,900
You saw it yourselves.

349
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,000
With my family's condition,

350
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,260
when could I ever afford a bike like that?

351
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,520
Take a look.

352
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:35,920
Which of these guys is

353
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,520
the 30-year-old Jia Xiaoze?

354
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:39,760
He's not here.

355
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,920
He's not here? Are you sure?

356
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:45,560
Then tell us

357
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:47,360
about your Brother Ze's

358
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,720
physical features.

359
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,120
His mouth, nose, face, whatever.

360
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:54,000
Every time he saw me, he wore

361
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,280
a mask

362
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:56,920
and a hat,

363
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,770
and sometimes sunglasses.

364
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,520
I just remember

365
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,840
his eyes slanted upwards

366
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,120
and were very bright.

367
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,280
That person's eyes slanted upwards,

368
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,240
and his eyelashes were very long.

369
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,440
Very long eyelashes.

370
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,720
That person's eyes

371
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,560
slanted upwards,

372
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,480
kind of like phoenix eyes.

373
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,520
And

374
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,980
his eyelashes were very long too.

375
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:23,880
I really can't remember anything else.

376
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:24,920
That's it?

377
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,280
Before, I always thought of him as

378
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,600
a fan of my cosplay.

379
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,600
Later, when he gave me money,

380
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,880
I started calling him brother.

381
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,720
Do you have his phone number?

382
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:34,560
Give it to us.

383
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:35,240
We'll check it.

384
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,160
Yes, yes, I have his number.

385
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,800
He just called me. Look.

386
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:42,560
What did he want?

387
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,200
He just asked if I was doing well
after getting out

388
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:47,640
and if I had any difficulties.

389
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:49,000
After all, he made me

390
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,400
pretend to be a traffic cop before...

391
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,120
I didn't even sell him out.

392
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,650
Pretty loyal, right? So...

393
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,520
You actually think you're being loyal?

394
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,440
Call him.

395
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,960
Tell him you need to see him
and ask him out.

396
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,720
You want me to lure him out

397
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,600
so you can catch him.

398
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,730
You've got quite the vocabulary, kid.

399
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,640
Listen to me.

400
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,170
Cooperate with us, hear me?

401
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:09,760
And another thing...

402
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,540
Captain Li,

403
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:17,820
come back quickly.

404
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:18,560
The fake traffic cop
from the night of the accident

405
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,420
turned himself in at the station.

406
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,560
Turned himself in?
